<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 7th Grade (CEFR: A2.2)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> Panama's Wildlife</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> The Daily Habits of Animals</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Contextualize basic classroom instructions supported with visual aids. Communication: Facilitate discussions on classroom rules.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can contextualize classroom instructions using visual aids (e.g., shows a picture of a jaguar for the instruction, "Choose your favorite animal.").
            Can facilitate a discussion on classroom rules by using simple gestures (e.g., making a "quiet" gesture for "no talking").
            Can support instructions with visual aids to help peers understand (e.g., points to a picture and says, "This is the jaguar's habitat. You have to write about it.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #e6e6e6;">
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Animal Sounds & Habits Charades (5 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows flashcards of Panama's wildlife (jaguar, sloth, harpy eagle, snake).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students make the animal sound or mime a daily habit (e.g., sloth moving slowly, eagle hunting).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher encourages peers to guess the animal and its habit. (e.g., "Is it a sloth? Does it move slowly?")</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> Mediating Instructions with Visuals and Gestures (5 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher presents a simple classroom instruction, e.g., "Choose your favorite animal." Teacher points to animal flashcards and gestures a "selection" motion.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher models how to support an instruction: "Draw a forest." (Teacher points to a picture of a forest and makes a drawing motion in the air).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher models pronunciation of "forest" (short 'o') and "eagle" (long 'e').</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> (3 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'Draw,' what do I do with my hand?" (Students mime drawing)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I show you a picture of a jaguar, do you think about a bird or a cat?" (Students point to a jaguar picture/say "cat")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 13 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Activity:</b> "Wildlife Habitat Tour Map" Instructions (7 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher displays a large, simple example of a "Wildlife Habitat Tour Map" (e.g., a basic drawing with a few elements like a river, forest, mountain).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher presents written instructions (on board/slides) for adding elements to the map, each paired with a visual icon (e.g., "Draw a forest HERE." with a tree icon; "Add a jaguar THERE." with a jaguar icon).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher uses "There is/there are" to describe the example map: "There is a river. There are many trees in the forest."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher emphasizes pronunciation of compound nouns like "wildlife" (wild-life).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Large example of a "Wildlife Habitat Tour Map," flashcards of animals/habitats, written instructions supported by visual icons.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpret basic written instructions supported by visual aids to describe environments.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Match the written instruction to the correct visual icon. (e.g., Match "Add an endangered species" to a picture of an endangered animal).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True/False: "There are <u>two</u> rivers on the map." (Students say true or false based on the example map).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 7 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Contextualizing instructions using "There is/there are," present simple for habits, comparative/superlative adjectives, and target vocabulary (habitat, forest, jaguar, predator, prey, species, adapt, protect, endangered, nocturnal, diverse).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b> (10 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Guided Instruction Mediation (Controlled Practice):</b> Teacher distributes a handout with simple instructions related to the map (e.g., "Add a prey animal," "Make the forest larger," "Draw a nocturnal animal"). Next to each instruction, there's a blank space. Students draw a simple visual aid (icon/gesture sketch) that explains the instruction. Teacher circulates, giving feedback on clarity. (e.g., For "Add a prey animal," student draws a tapir/deer. For "Make the forest larger," student draws a small tree and a big tree with an arrow).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Picture-to-Sentence Mediation (Semi-controlled):</b> Teacher shows a picture of an animal (e.g., a jaguar). Students, in pairs, give an instruction using "This is..." or "There is..." and a present simple verb describing its habit. (e.g., "This is a jaguar. It hunts quickly."). Then, using a picture of another animal (e.g., sloth), they create a comparative sentence: "The jaguar is faster than the sloth." They practice syllable division with words like "nocturnal" (noc-tur-nal).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer-Instruction & Clarification (Pair Interaction):</b> Students work in pairs. Each student has a basic, blank outline of a habitat map. Student A gives Student B three instructions to add elements to their map (e.g., "Draw a river here," "There are many diverse species on this side," "Add the largest predator in the jungle"). Student A must support each instruction with a visual aid (a small sketch or a gesture) to help Student B understand. Student B follows the instructions and then gives Student A three instructions using the same technique. They use "this/that" to refer to specific areas.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 10 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Activity:</b> "Wildlife Habitat Tour Map" Mediation Challenge (10 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students form small groups (3-4 students). Each group has a shared, partially completed "Wildlife Habitat Tour Map" (from previous lessons or a new one provided by the teacher).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One student in the group (the "Mediator") receives a secret list of 3-4 instructions to add to the map (e.g., "Add an endangered species of bird," "Draw a resilient plant," "Show where jaguars hunt," "Describe the fastest animal here").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Mediator must explain these instructions to their group members, using only simple language, visual aids (pointing to areas on the map, quick sketches on a mini-whiteboard/paper), and gestures. They cannot show the written instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The group members listen to the Mediator and draw/label the elements on their shared map. They can ask for clarification, but the Mediator must re-explain using different visuals or simpler words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher observes groups, focusing on the Mediator's ability to contextualize instructions and the group's ability to follow. Emphasis on the pronunciation of long and short vowel sounds in vocabulary like "snake" (/sneɪk/) and "frog" (/frɒg/).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">This activity directly integrates the 21st Century Skills Project, with students actively designing their habitat map through mediated instructions.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 10 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist & Peer Assessment (7 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> "Map Mediator Presentation"</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group selects one "Mediator" to present a specific section of their completed "Wildlife Habitat Tour Map" to another group or the teacher.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Mediator explains 2-3 key features of that habitat section (e.g., "Here is the forest where jaguars live," "There are many diverse species here," "This sloth moves slowly").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They must support their explanation with visual aids (pointing to the map, simple gestures for actions/locations) to ensure the audience understands. They use comparatives like "The river is longer than this path."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Peers use a simple checklist to rate the Mediator's clarity, use of visuals, and effective communication.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of mediated explanation (easy to understand instructions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of visual aids and gestures to support understanding.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (habitat, forest, species, adapt) and grammar (there is/are, present simple, comparatives).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of key words (long/short vowels, syllable division).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and facilitation of group discussion.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> (2 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What helped you most to understand your classmates' instructions today (pictures, gestures, simple words)?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new word or phrase you used to describe your habitat map?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 9 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b> (2 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did using visuals and gestures make it easier for you to explain things today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one challenge you faced when trying to explain a part of your map to your group, and how did you overcome it?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> (2 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What mediation strategies worked best for students to contextualize instructions and facilitate discussions? Was the use of visual aids effective?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Were students able to integrate the grammar (comparatives, there is/are) and vocabulary naturally? What adjustments or additional scaffolds (e.g., more gesture modeling, simpler visuals) are needed for future mediation tasks or if this lesson were to be repeated?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> (1 min)</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">This lesson concludes the theme on "The Daily Habits of Animals" and the "Wildlife Habitat Tour Map" project, bringing together all four skills (listening, reading, speaking, writing) through mediation. The next unit will introduce a new theme and scenario, starting with listening and vocabulary.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time: 5 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>